 R←Test_Select_006(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;⎕IO;⎕ML;list;qdmx;value
⍝ Exercise "Select" with two integers (min max) rather than a Boolean as `manyFlag`.
⍝ Only the checks carried out on the left argument and automation are exercised here:
⍝ the selection itself needs a user, see "Test_Select_012".
⍝ The syntax was introduced in 2.1.0
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 ⎕IO←1 ⋄ ⎕ML←1
 R←T._Failed

 list←'One' 'Two' 'Three' 'Four' 'Five'

 ⍝ Invalid specifications of "manyFlag":
 :For value :In (0 2)(3 2)(2 6)(2 2.5)(,2)('x')
     :Trap 11
         {}('Select two:'value)C.Select list
         →T.GoToTidyUp 1
     :Else
         qdmx←⎕DMX
         →T.GoToTidyUp 11≠qdmx.EN
     :EndTrap
 :EndFor

 ⍝ Valid ones; note that automation is restricted by neither "manyFlag" nor (min max):
 C.AddAutomation'Select' 'Select two:'(2 4)
 →T.GoToTidyUp 2 4≢('Select two:'(2 2))C.Select list
 →T.GoToTidyUp 2 4≢('Select two:'(2 2)1)C.Select list

 1 C.AddAutomation'Select' 'Select two:'(1 2 3)
 →T.GoToTidyUp 1 2 3≢('Select two:'(2 2))C.Select list

 1 C.AddAutomation'Select' 'Select two:'(4 4 1)  ⍝ Duplicates are removed
 →T.GoToTidyUp 4 1≢('Select two:'(2 2))C.Select list

 1 C.AddAutomation'Select' 'Select two:' 5
 →T.GoToTidyUp 5≢('Select two:'(1 5))C.Select list

 R←T._OK

∆TidyUp:
 C.Cleanup
⍝Done
